//! Occitan conjugation (Languedocien standard). Occitan is a Romance
//! language cited by its infinitive, with person/number agreement across a
//! rich synthetic paradigm. Two conjugation classes are genuinely
//! productive and generated by rule from the bare stem (the infinitive
//! minus its final two characters):
//!
//!   * the -ar class (parlar → parl-): present -i/-as/-a/-am/-atz/-an,
//!     imperfect -av-, preterite -èr-, future -ar-, conditional -ari-,
//!     present subjunctive -e, imperfect subjunctive -èss-, the three
//!     imperatives, the -at past participle and the -ant gerund;
//!   * the inchoative -ir class (brandir → brand-): the -iss-/-isc-/-iguèr-
//!     augmented paradigm.
//!
//! Everything else — the athematic -er/-re verbs (véser, saber, voler),
//! the short -ir verbs (dormir, venir) and every stem/spelling
//! irregularity of an -ar or -ir verb — carries an explicit form in
//! `data/oci/parts.tsv`, mined from the agreement of the two oracles
//! (UniMorph ∩ kaikki.org). Verified against two oracles.

